Subject: [run 2] stage admission from the config, not from the stage's name

UNAPPLIED. Do not apply while run 1 is on the GPU: it modifies the source of a
live job, and the assertion worth making about that run is precisely that its
source was unmodified while it trained (reports/decorative_guards.md, "A
corollary about fixing things"). Apply after run 1 has written its final
checkpoint and that checkpoint's provenance has been read back.

WHAT IT CHANGES
  FoundationTrainer.run_stage decides what a stage sees with six tests on
  `stage.name`. Two gate source admission and are the reason refusal X06 fires
  on an integrity-ordered config; four more were found while preparing run 2
  and matter because run 2's stages are NOT named I_regional..V_individual:

    line 303  STAGE_PERMISSIONS.get(stage.name, ("*",))   the gradient allowlist
              -- the default is PERMISSIVE. An unrecognised stage name gets no
              restriction at all, so every per-stage mask in the corrected
              curriculum would have silently widened.
    line 498  stage.name == "I_regional"                  boundary randomisation
    line 510  stage.name in ("IV_assembly",)              haemodynamic rollout
    line 585  stage.name == "V_individual"                build the Individualizer
    line 613  stage.name != "V_individual"                admit SIMULATED sources
    line 617  stage.name in ("III_sliced", ...)           admit MEASURED sources

  and one defect behind them that only an integrity ordering exposes:

    line 543  the tier-3 `anatomical_prior` loss is composed inside sim_losses,
              so it is emitted only on a step where the SIMULATED loader ran.
              Run 2's T3_population_prior admits tiers 1,2,3 and not 4, so on
              the unpatched trainer that stage would emit no tier-3 loss at all
              -- it would admit the population prior in name only. Moved to
              FoundationTrainer.anat_losses().

  It also wires curriculum_admission.assert_region_count into __init__, because
  cfg.model.n_regions is read by nothing in the run path (SCWBD takes its shape
  from anat.n_regions) and is therefore free to name a parcellation the model
  never loaded -- which is exactly what "n_regions: 454  # Schaefer-400 + 32 +
  22" did for the whole of run 1.

BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY
  stage_admission(..., strict=False) falls back to curriculum_admission's
  transcription of run 1's five stage names, so configs/scwbd_001_beta.yaml
  behaves identically and its checkpoint stays resumable. A NEW stage name with
  no `extra.curriculum` block raises UndeclaredStage rather than defaulting --
  the previous default granted everything, so an unwired stage and a
  fully-permitted stage read the same.

DEPENDS ON
  scwbd/foundation/curriculum_admission.py  (new, committed separately)
  scwbd/foundation/anatomy.py at f816f2a    (branch wt/turing; NOT on master)

BASE -- ORDERING MATTERS, and this was checked rather than assumed
  Apply f816f2a FIRST, then this. Verified with `git apply --check`:

    master 3400cee..508ae5e with f816f2a applied  -> applies clean
    master 3400cee / 508ae5e, pristine            -> REFUSED,
        "error: patch failed: scwbd/foundation/train.py:194"

  because f816f2a rewrites the `self.anat = ...` block immediately above this
  patch's first hunk, so the context does not match without it. This is a real
  dependency, not a merge artifact: `assert_region_count` compares
  cfg.model.n_regions against the loaded anatomy, and on pristine master the
  loaded anatomy is always the 454-region synthetic prior, so the assertion
  would refuse the run-2 config on every invocation.

  train.py, config.py and scwbd/curriculum/ are byte-identical between 3400cee
  and 508ae5e (`git diff --stat 3400cee 508ae5e -- ...` is empty), so every
  verdict quoted here holds at both.

TEST
  tests/foundation/test_curriculum_admission.py -- 11 tests.
  Watched to fail: 7 fail against 3400cee, 11 pass with this patch applied.
  The 4 that pass in both worlds are marked in that file's docstring, because a
  test that cannot fail is not evidence.

VALIDATOR
  With this patch and f816f2a, `python -m scwbd.curriculum validate
  configs/run2/scwbd-001.yaml` returns ACCEPTED. Note that X06 does not "pass":
  removing the gates makes scwbd.curriculum.legacy.reconstruct_stage_admission
  raise GateNotFound, so X06 is reported NOT EVALUABLE. That is the honest
  reading -- there is no longer a trainer gate to contradict the config -- but
  it is a hole where a check used to be, and legacy.py (not this patch's owner)
  should learn to recognise config-driven admission positively.

